  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced></msup></math></p><p>Now differentiating the function to find function is increasing or decreasing,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>is decreasing function on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The absolute maximum value of the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
